On data node 1, block sending signals to API node 12
HeartbeatIntervalDbApi is configured on both 'global'
section (2000ms) and API node 12 section (5000ms)
sleep 10 sec (more than 3 * the global HeartbeatIntervalDbApi),
to show that the global HeartbeatIntervalDbApi is not in use (node is not disconnected)
include/assert_grep.inc [No cleanup of node 12 connection state in the log]
sleep 10 sec more (10sec + 10sec > 3 * the API node HeartbeatIntervalDbApi),
the missing of 3 heartbeats will trigger the node to disconnect
include/assert_grep.inc [Cleanup of node 12 connection state in the log]
On data node 1, resume sending signals to API node 12
Now, let's test communication in the opposite direction
On data node 1, block receiving signals from API node 11
sleep 10 sec (more than 3 * the global HeartbeatIntervalDbApi),
to show that the global HeartbeatIntervalDbApi is not in use (node is not disconnected)
include/assert_grep.inc [No cleanup of node 11 connection state in the log]
sleep 20 sec more (20sec + 10sec > 4 * the API node HeartbeatIntervalDbApi),
the missing of 4 heartbeats will trigger the node to disconnect
include/assert_grep.inc [Cleanup of node 11 connection state in the log]
On data node 1, resume receiving signals from API node 11
